{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/39890-reconciling-ends-of-empire-and-orpheus","id":39890,"title":"Reconciling 'Ends Of Empire' and 'Orpheus'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T03:29:11-08:00","id":39890,"title":"Reconciling 'Ends Of Empire' and 'Orpheus'","content":"The Sixth Great Maelstrom sweeps across the Underworld, and it is a <i>doozy</i>. The city of Stygia is attacked by the servants of Oblivion and abandoned. We know these to be true. What happens next has two different stories.<br /> <br /> <i>Ends of Empire</i> has Stygia fall in the wake of the Spectre attack and Charon's Transcendence. The state of the wider Dark Kingdom of Iron is uncertain, but even in a worst-case scenario, the various Necropoli could survive as city-states in the Shadowlands. If the trend is followed (this is not a given, considering that unique nature of the Sixth Great Maelstrom), then the Maelstrom will eventually peter itself out.<br /> <br /> <i>Orpheus</i> has things quite a bit more catastrophic. The relic nuke detonates, blowing forth the Great Maelstrom. The force of the storm shunts the dead into or through the Shroud, creating the Stormwall in its place. An endless storm of debris engulfs the uninhabited Shadowlands, now empty save for Spectres. The dead that survive persist in the Skinlands, invisible to the living.<br /> <br /> The easy answer is that the Sixth Great Maelstrom transpires as seen in <i>Ends of Empire</i> and intensifies rather than slowing down, eventually reaching the frenzied state it's at in Orpheus. While this does lead to a less dramatic nudging of the dead through the Shroud rather than one intense explosion, it does easily bridge the two. <br /> <br /> Either take leaves the Isle of Sorrows empty of the dead, free to be discovered as the Nameless City in <i>End Game</i>. Would other Necropoli survive? What of the other Dark Kingdoms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:37:40-08:00","id":40031,"title":"","content":"In such a case, I think most of the other Dark Kingdoms would be screwed, with the exception of the Dark Kingdom of Sand (Egypt's underworld) and maybe the Dark Kingdom of Jade. Anubis is among the strongest beings in the Underworld, and between him and Osiris it seems extremely possible that the Dark Kingdom would survive, albeit with major damage. <br /> <br /> As for the Dark Kingdom of Jade it's located extremely close to Yomi-wan. It's possible that the 1000 Hells would give the Dark Kingdom and its necropolises enough stability to survive the Maelstrom in some form. Furthermore, Emperor Qin Shihuang is a Neverborn, so that might give him considerable power to direct or temper the Maelstrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T11:00:03-08:00","id":40064,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Wr20 will address this is some manner. <br /> <br /> In any case, how does the Dark Kingdom of Sand match up with the old Mummy? Also, what makes anyone believe 1000 Hells or Emperor Qin Shihuang would do anything to help anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:28:25-08:00","id":40105,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Duat (the Dark Kingdom of Sand) was prominantly featured in <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b>. In particular, the notion there was that the Ghost Storm woke Osiris, and he issued a decree to his followers, the earlier-edition mummies, to sacrifice themselves so that the <b>Resurrection</b>-style mummies could be born.<br /> <br /> I tend to agree that the Sixth Great Maelstrom would probably shatter virtually every Dark Kingdom, and would do a number on the Far Shores as well. IMHO though, the real difficulty in reconciling <b>End of Empire</b> and <b>Orpheus</b> is that the latter posits that the ghost storm wiped out the entire wraith population: by the time Orpheus begins, there are no ghosts older than five years (when the Storm hit). This is necessary for Orpheus\u2019 plot, as otherwise it would be easy to just find an older ghost and ask him what happened five years ago: mystery solved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-31-2013, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:36:43-08:00","id":40426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/39890-reconciling-ends-of-empire-and-orpheus?p=40031#post40031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In such a case, I think most of the other Dark Kingdoms would be screwed, with the exception of the Dark Kingdom of Sand (Egypt's underworld) and maybe the Dark Kingdom of Jade. Anubis is among the strongest beings in the Underworld, and between him and Osiris it seems extremely possible that the Dark Kingdom would survive, albeit with major damage.<br /> <br /> As for the Dark Kingdom of Jade it's located extremely close to Yomi-wan. It's possible that the 1000 Hells would give the Dark Kingdom and its necropolises enough stability to survive the Maelstrom in some form. Furthermore, Emperor Qin Shihuang is a Neverborn, so that might give him considerable power to direct or temper the Maelstrom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Kingdom of Sand has the potential to be a new haven with the reborn helping out. They have insane magics that can provide for an empire in such a way that they don't have to rely on Soulforging! If they advertised they would get a lot of converts, and they have agents in the form of the Reborn around the world.<br /> <br /> I got the feeling in revised that they made the Underworld ravaged in ruins, but they did it in such a way you could still use ghosts in your games, because ghosts at least would find shelter in haunts. And if you had a game that allowed for travel in the Underworld you likely also had amazing Magics in the Underworld that Ghosts don't have, even werewolf for instance with a relatively minor amount of Underworld magic has access to relatively weak items for them that provide insane boosts in the Underworld, like the Stormcloak for traveling through the Maelstroms, and Jack-O-Lanterns able to trap ghosts.<br /> <br /> In many games they encourage you to either fix the local Underworld or carve out an empire yourself. This is especially prominent in Demon and Mummy. For instance a Mummy could use magics to provide a steady supply of Paper and ammo and other things ghosts can't rely on, as well as send a Yacht or a Mansion to the Underworld! And Demons have great control over Souls and Underworld travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:12:22-08:00","id":40727,"title":"","content":"I prefer using the post-<b>End of Empire</b> Wraith as a way to play wraiths without messing with gargantuan Dark Kingdoms and Underworld politics, focusing instead on the interaction between wraiths and the living; so I\u2019m partial t the notion that the Underworld is a mess, and that a new Kingdom of Iron/Sand/whatever won\u2019t be rising to \u201cprovide stability\u201d anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}